      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Artificial sweeteners are a ubiquitous commodity on the market. The idea that people can consume a sweet food or beverage with \"zero\" calories seems too good to be true, and perhaps it is. The longevity and abundance of these products on the market necessitate the study of their mechanisms and their relationships to health and disease, including possible links to obesity, cardiovascular disease, and diabetes."},
